+### Transferring a user between organizations
+
+- Only org admins of the organization in the path may transfer a user; other
+  members of that organization get 403. An organization other than the
+  caller's is not visible → 404.
+- The user must belong to the organization in the path (otherwise 404).
+  `toOrgId` must be non-empty, differ from the current organization (400),
+  and name an existing organization (400). Organizations have no table: one
+  exists when some user belongs to it.
+- The transfer is all or nothing. The user's memberships in the old
+  organization's projects are removed, and tasks they hold in those projects
+  are unassigned, because project members must belong to the project's
+  organization. The user's org admin rights are dropped (they are per
+  organization).
+
